.TH CIRCQ_TIMED_SEND_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
circq_timed_send_zc \- send with timeout
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t circq_timed_send_zc(circular_queue *cq,
                                   c_message_t *msg,
                                   struct timespec *timeout);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Blocks up to the specified timeout waiting for space. If space becomes
available, sends the message and transfers ownership. If timeout expires
or sending is disabled, returns with appropriate error code.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cq       Circular queue to send to
msg      Message to send (data ownership transfers on success)
timeout  Relative timeout duration
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success              - Message sent successfully
ccol_invalid_args         - cq or msg is NULL, or msg validation fails
ccol_not_permitted        - Sending has been disabled
ccol_timed_out            - Timeout expired
ccol_unexpected_failure   - System error (check errno)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Blocks up to timeout duration
After waking, rechecks if sending is still enabled
On failure, caller retains ownership of msg->data
Uses CLOCK_REALTIME for timeout calculations
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR circq_send_zc (3),
.BR circq_try_send_zc (3)
